fair competition that  is probably started by China but  potentially also by some other countries  um to sign up sum up thanks to the  single Market we live love study and  work all over Europe across borders so  how could citizens cross-border rights  could be improved or strengthened  further  very important because for me I have to  say the most important part of the  European Union and also of the single  Market is the citizens at the end  everything we do everything we try to  achieve it's for the sake of a citizen  so yeah citizens rights are really  really really important and there is big  and small measures one I find  small but also really really important  one of my green colleagues is working on  it it is a statute for basically  European associations that if citizens  from both sides of the Border they want  to found an association they can just do  it because at the moment this is quite  difficult so there's still very very  important small and bigger steps where  we can improve basically the rights of  of EU citizens perfect  thank you so much for your time today it  was a pleasure to have you here and  thank you and to all our followers for  tuning in once again have a good evening  and yeah have a good evening as well  thank you
 

